=== GAME STATE MACHINE ===

WAITING
  → any RFID tap on any side → PLAYERS_REGISTERING

PLAYERS_REGISTERING
  → A slot 1 AND B slot 1 both filled → GAME_PLAYING (auto, no button)
  → additional players can tap in at any point (join as slot 2)
  → if a player deregisters and one side becomes empty → stay REGISTERING

GAME_PLAYING
  → either side reaches live_tables.max_score goals → GAME_OVER
  → ALL players on one side deregister → ABANDONED
      (no grace period — immediate stop when a full side empties)
  → second player can tap in mid-game (joins slot 2 of their side)
  → second player can deregister mid-game (removed from slot 2)
  → slot 1 player can deregister mid-game IF there is a slot 2 player
      (slot 2 becomes slot 1, game continues)
  → slot 1 player deregisters with NO slot 2 player → ABANDONED

GAME_OVER
  → save complete match to history (once, deduplicated by session_id)
  → state stays GAME_OVER until any RFID tap → WAITING

ABANDONED
  → save partial match with result_type = "abandoned"
  → state → WAITING immediately

Mode assignment (dynamic, updated whenever live_players changes):
  both sides have 1 player  → mode = "1v1"
  both sides have 2 players → mode = "2v2"
  mixed (1 vs 2)            → mode = "mixed"
  Mixed is valid — game proceeds normally.

=== RFID BEHAVIOR ===

On any RFID tap received (tablefootball/table/<id>/rfid):

1. Look up UID in players table.
   If not found: create new guest (Guest1, Guest2, ... GuestN).

2. Log to rfid_events.

3. Check if UID already in live_players for this table:

   YES (player already registered):
     → Deregister logic:
       If state is GAME_PLAYING:
         If this is the last player on their side:
           → remove from live_players → ABANDONED
         If their side has another player:
           → remove this player (slot reassigned)
           → game continues
       If state is PLAYERS_REGISTERING or WAITING:
         → remove from live_players
         → if one side now empty → no state change needed
       Log event_type = "deregister"

   NO (new registration):
     → Find first empty slot on the tapping side (slot 1, then slot 2).
     → If both slots full: ignore tap, log event_type = "ignored".
     → Add to live_players.
     → Check auto-start condition (A slot 1 AND B slot 1 filled).
     → If met and state != GAME_PLAYING: → GAME_PLAYING.
     → Log event_type = "register"

4. After any change:
   → Publish tablefootball/pico/<pico_id>/player (response to Pico)
   → Publish tablefootball/table/<table_id>/sync (to all Picos)
   → Push SSE update to all browsers

=== MQTT PROTOCOL ===

Every payload includes:
  "v": 1
  "ts": <unix_ms>   (server overwrites with its own timestamp on receipt)

QoS levels:
  heartbeat          → QoS 0
  rfid               → QoS 1
  state              → QoS 1
  ball_position      → QoS 0   (lossy fine, high frequency)
  table sync         → QoS 1, retain=true
  players_list       → QoS 1, retain=true

LWT per Pico:
  topic:   tablefootball/pico/<pico_id>/status
  payload: {"pico_id":"<id>", "online":false, "reason":"lwt"}
  retain:  true, qos: 1

