=== SSE EVENTS ===

Endpoint: GET /events  (text/event-stream)

Event types:

  event: table_state
  data: {"table_id":1, "state":"GAME_PLAYING", "score_a":3, "score_b":2,
         "mode":"mixed", "max_score":10, "fastest":12.4,
         "team_a":[...], "team_b":[...]}

  event: ball_position
  data: {"table_id":1, "x":320, "y":180, "speed":14.2}
  (NOT stored in DB — broadcast only)

  event: player_update
  data: {"players": [...]}

  event: pico_status
  data: {"pico_id":"table1-left", "online":true}

Ball position SSE behavior:
  - Only broadcast when table state is GAME_PLAYING.
  - If SSE client queue is full (max 20 items), drop ball_position events.
  - Never drop table_state, player_update, or pico_status events.

